SAVE - save memory to a file››Syntax:› SAVE [d:][path]file[.ext]›      [$]start [$]end››Writes the memory from start to end›(both included) to a binary load file.›With LOAD, it turns a file with many›segments into one, or saves a memory›snapshot. Numbers are decimal; $ means›hex.››Example:› SAVE TEST.DAT $4000 $4007››See also: LOAD, BLOAD›